OL,3,GNEWSAIrish army received warning day
OL,4,Abefore Omagh bomb, inquiry told
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Omagh Bombing Inquiry has heard
OL,7,Fthat an Irish army camp received a
OL,8,Fwarning that the town was to be the
OL,9,Ftarget of a bomb the day before the
OL,10,Ffatal explosion.
OL,12,FIt was revealed during evidence from
OL,13,Fthe journalist John Ware who has
OL,14,Freported extensively on the bombing.
OL,15,FWare said the information about the
OL,16,Fcall was given to him by the counsel
OL,17,Ffor the bombing inquiry in preparation
OL,18,Ffor giving evidence.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
